After {{ p.withdrawal }}, data are anonymised and integrated into the analysis, so individual contributions can no longer be identified or removed. Data already included in aggregated analyses or publications cannot be removed from them. {% if d.has_audio %}Recordings are deleted after transcription, so withdrawal after that point applies to the anonymised transcript. {% endif %}{% if d.methods | selectattr("key", "in", ["focus_group", "co_design", "creative_workshop"]) | list %}Contributions to group discussions cannot always be fully separated from those of others; the participant's own contributions are removed from transcripts where possible. {% endif %}Consent records are kept as evidence of consent even if a participant withdraws. This is explained in the information sheet and consent form.
